-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cataclysm high-end catalogue -- 4477 items at NATIVE stat values
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Every armour piece, weapon, trinket, ring, neck, cloak and shield in the Cata
-- 4.3.4 client at item level 346-416, rare quality or better. All of them already
-- exist in item_template as appearance shells from the Wraith downport, carrying
-- the right name, class, quality and slot and ZERO of everything else. This fills
-- them in.
--
-- NO RESCALE. Stats are Blizzard's own values for each item, untouched. The
-- "item level 428 and upwards" progression comes from the DYNAMIC upgrade system
-- that is already live, not from scaled clones:
--   * ItemUpgradeManager::GetItemTier resolves a tier purely from ItemLevel,
--     with no class or quality gate, so writing the item level below is all that
--     is needed to make these upgradeable.
--   * dc_item_upgrade_tiers: ilvl 300-411 -> tier 4 (10 steps, x1.5 max),
--     ilvl 412+ -> tier 5 (15 steps, x1.6 max, max_ilvl 0 = unbounded).
--   * ItemUpgradeStatApplication.cpp applies the per-item stat_multiplier at
--     equip time. The retired clone model (dc_item_templates_upgrade, empty) is
--     deliberately NOT used -- clones are the ones that equip without a client
--     item id and break links, compare and transmog.
--
-- WHY NATIVE AND NOT RESCALED TO 428. Item level on this realm does not track
-- stat budget: the existing ilvl-500 and ilvl-510 gear carries LOWER primary
-- stats (avg 174 and 206) than these Cata items do at ilvl 359 (avg 269).
-- Rescaling to Blizzard's ilvl-428 stat budget would have produced avg primary
-- 455 against a live band of roughly 180-280 -- about twice the realm's current
-- best in slot. Native values land these at the top of the existing band and let
-- the upgrade ladder take them from there.
--
-- SOURCE -- Cata 4.3.4 DBFilesClient/Item-sparse.db2 (WDB2, build 15595) read
-- through the wow-update-enUS-15211/15354/15595 StormLib patch chain, plus
-- Item.db2 for class/subclass/slot. Layout verified against the live DB: item
-- 51130 reads back ilvl 264, req 80, quality 4, slot 3, set 898.
--
-- ARMOUR is curve-derived, not stored:
--   floor(ItemArmorQuality[ilvl][quality] * ItemArmorTotal[ilvl][armour type]
--         * ArmorLocation[slot][armour type])
-- validated on stock ilvl-264 plate to within a point (51130 -> 1981 vs 1980
-- stored, 51216 -> 2311 vs 2310). ArmorLocation[20] (robe) is all zeros, so robes
-- take the chest slot -- without that every robe ships with no armour at all.
--
-- WEAPON DAMAGE is curve-derived too:
--   dps = ItemDamage<Type>[ilvl][quality];  avg = dps * delay / 1000
--   dmg_min/max = avg * (1 -/+ DmgVariance/2)
-- Reproduces stock 3.3.5 exactly or within one point (50654 -> 263/489 exact,
-- 47528 -> 394/732 exact). DmgVariance is the Item-sparse field commonly
-- mislabelled StatScalingFactor -- pinned here by matching five stock weapons
-- with known variances of 0.4 / 0.5 / 0.6, all five agreeing.
--
-- THE ONE INFERENCE IN THIS FILE: which weapons use the Caster damage curve.
-- Blizzard selects ItemDamage*Caster (exactly half the physical dps) for weapons
-- carrying Intellect, and 3.3.5 cannot confirm it because Cataclysm rebalanced
-- caster weapon damage outright (a WotLK caster one-hand at ilvl 264 does 131 dps
-- where the Cata caster curve says 113). 112 of the 547 weapons here are treated as
-- caster weapons on the "has Intellect or Spell Power" rule. If that is wrong for
-- an item its damage is out by 2x in one direction; flip is_caster() in
-- emit_highend.py and regenerate.
--
-- WOTLK-ONLY STATS: Item-sparse stat types 49 (Mastery) and 50 (bonus armour)
-- have no 3.3.5 equivalent -- the ITEM_MOD enum stops at 48. 1370 such stats are
-- DROPPED rather than remapped, so the affected items carry one stat fewer.
-- Substituting crit or haste for mastery would be a balance decision rather than
-- a downport. To change it, edit DROPPED_STATS in emit_highend.py.
--
-- Durability comes from the modal MaxDurability of stock ilvl>=200 gear of the
-- same (class, subclass, InventoryType). Thrown weapons get 0, which is what 72
-- of the 74 stock thrown weapons carry.
--
-- Does NOT touch `itemset` (file 01 owns it), `name`, `class`, `subclass`,
-- `Quality`, `InventoryType` or `displayid` (all already correct from the
-- downport). 432 of these items are also covered by 03_cata_itemset_item_stats.sql;
-- both files derive from the same source with the same code so the values are
-- identical and the order of application does not matter. 03 is still needed for
-- the set items BELOW ilvl 346, which this file does not select.
--
-- FIELD VALIDATION -- several Cata columns use id spaces 3.3.5 does not have, and
-- ObjectMgr::LoadItemTemplates warns and zeroes them at load. Corrected here
-- instead, against the very stores the server checks:
--   ItemLimitCategory      3.3.5 has ids 2-85; Cata uses 89-198
--   RandomSuffix           ItemRandomSuffix.dbc has 5-99; Cata uses 417-465, and
--                          417-441 have no item_enchantment_template rows at all
--                          while 456-465 resolve to ench ids outside the dbc
--   RequiredReputationFaction  Faction.dbc ends at 1171; Cata uses 1172-1178
--   socketColor            masked to META|RED|YELLOW|BLUE (15); Cata sends 32
--   BagFamily / TotemCategory / GemProperties  checked against their dbcs
-- Material and Sheath are taken from our own client Item.dbc, because that is what
-- the server compares them against -- NOT from the Cata source they were read from.
-- Corrections applied: BagFamily 1, ItemLimitCategory 203, Material <- Item.dbc 3, RandomSuffix 72, RequiredReputationFaction 91, sheath <- Item.dbc 156, socketColor 14
--
-- Idempotent. UPDATE only, so an entry missing from item_template is a silent
-- no-op -- the verification block at the bottom will surface any.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- item levels present: 346, 350, 352, 353, 358, 359, 365, 371, 372, 377, 378, 379, 384, 390, 391, 397, 403, 410, 416
-- slot split: armour 3071, cloak 146, neck 147, ring 203, shield 49, trinket 314, weapon 547

